1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,212
Every night, from dusk to dawn,
priests walked through an

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:07,292
Ethiopian emperor's palace,
sprinkling holy water.

3
00:00:07,742 --> 00:00:11,646
Not for a feast. For protection.
He was afraid of magicians.

4
00:00:12,096 --> 00:00:19,840
His name was Zara Yaqob, and
he ruled from 1434 to 1468.

5
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:24,194
Few rulers in Ethiopian
history fought magic so hard.

6
00:00:24,644 --> 00:00:28,079
And his own chronicle can't agree
on what his reign was like.

7
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:35,431
Born around 1399, Zara Yaqob spent
his youth locked away on Amba

8
00:00:35,431 --> 00:00:39,735
Geshen, the mountain where
royal princes were kept.

9
00:00:40,185 --> 00:00:43,771
He became emperor in 1434, but waited two

10
00:00:43,771 --> 00:00:46,308
years to be crowned at Aksum.

11
00:00:46,758 --> 00:00:49,331
He wrote books of
theology, and his reforms

12
00:00:49,331 --> 00:00:51,366
still shape the Church's calendar.

13
00:00:51,816 --> 00:00:54,371
He wore an icon of the Virgin Mary, and

14
00:00:54,371 --> 00:00:56,467
ordered altars dedicated to her.

15
00:00:56,917 --> 00:01:00,501
The Senkesar remembers him
as orthodox and apostolic.

16
00:01:00,951 --> 00:01:04,065
So why do some pages of his
chronicle speak of terror?

17
00:01:06,015 --> 00:01:09,640
Zara Yaqob declared magical
prayers and sacrifices to

18
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:12,991
spirits to be devil worship,
punishable by death.

19
00:01:13,441 --> 00:01:16,919
He ordered talismans and
magical writings destroyed.

20
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:20,048
One scholar writes that no group was more

21
00:01:20,048 --> 00:01:22,531
feared or hated by him than magicians.

22
00:01:22,981 --> 00:01:25,134
The chronicle says his people had to carry

23
00:01:25,134 --> 00:01:26,672
a written vow on their bodies:

24
00:01:27,122 --> 00:01:30,407
I reject the accursed one.
I am a servant of Mary.

25
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:34,847
Was he fighting superstition, or
something he believed was real?

26
00:01:36,797 --> 00:01:40,231
Historian Steven Kaplan says
he believed it was real.

27
00:01:40,681 --> 00:01:43,528
Kaplan writes that he seems
to have lived in fear

28
00:01:43,528 --> 00:01:46,143
that his enemies would
use magic against him.

29
00:01:46,593 --> 00:01:49,493
He never doubted that a
charm could have power. What

30
00:01:49,493 --> 00:01:51,947
he condemned was where
that power came from.

31
00:01:52,397 --> 00:01:54,435
And that fear left a mark on his own

32
00:01:54,435 --> 00:01:56,813
chronicle, which survives in two versions.

33
00:01:58,763 --> 00:02:02,144
Zara Yaqob's chronicle,
version one: great terror and

34
00:02:02,144 --> 00:02:04,950
great fear spread through
the whole country.

35
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,772
Those who confessed to worshipping
the devil were punished,

36
00:02:08,772 --> 00:02:11,459
and it says he did not
even spare his own sons.

37
00:02:11,909 --> 00:02:15,026
Version two, copied into
the same book, says a great

38
00:02:15,026 --> 00:02:17,605
peace and great tranquility
spread instead,

39
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:20,888
because the king taught
justice and faith. It even

40
00:02:20,888 --> 00:02:23,324
counts him among the
prophets and apostles.

41
00:02:23,774 --> 00:02:26,611
Same emperor. Same book.
Which one is true?

42
00:02:28,561 --> 00:02:30,907
Did you know? The
chronicle says a cross of

43
00:02:30,907 --> 00:02:32,871
light appeared in the sky above him.

44
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:36,154
It came weeks after a
group of dissenting monks

45
00:02:36,154 --> 00:02:38,505
was executed, and he read it as a sign.

46
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:41,294
Where he saw it, he built a capital: Debre

47
00:02:41,294 --> 00:02:42,965
Berhan, the Mountain of Light.

48
00:02:43,415 --> 00:02:47,054
Some historians think
the light was Halley's

49
00:02:47,054 --> 00:02:50,114
comet, which crossed the sky in 1456.

50
00:02:52,064 --> 00:02:55,597
Around 1441, in this
same reign, the Church

51
00:02:55,597 --> 00:02:58,144
compiled the Book of the Pearl.

52
00:02:58,594 --> 00:03:01,082
Its purpose, in its own words: healing

53
00:03:01,082 --> 00:03:03,309
from spiritual and bodily illness.

54
00:03:03,759 --> 00:03:06,356
Remember the healing
scrolls from our debtera

55
00:03:06,356 --> 00:03:08,665
story? This was the Church's own answer.

56
00:03:09,115 --> 00:03:11,714
No charm at all: the
prayer of the priests,

57
00:03:11,714 --> 00:03:13,830
and olive oil poured over the sick.

58
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,446
It echoes the letter of
James: Is any sick among you?

59
00:03:17,446 --> 00:03:19,955
let him call for the elders of the church.

60
00:03:20,405 --> 00:03:22,683
So how should we remember the emperor who

61
00:03:22,683 --> 00:03:24,629
left us both the fear and the cure?

62
00:03:26,579 --> 00:03:29,868
Zara Yaqob was a devout
scholar, a reformer, and

63
00:03:29,868 --> 00:03:32,403
a ruler who answered fear with force.

64
00:03:32,853 --> 00:03:35,520
We traced his story to
his chronicle, in both

65
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,485
versions, and to the scholars
who read it closely.

66
00:03:38,935 --> 00:03:41,1000
So when a post hands you
a simple hero or a simple

67
00:03:41,1000 --> 00:03:44,268
villain, ask which version they read.

68
00:03:44,718 --> 00:03:47,235
And when fear knocks at
your own door, what then?

69
00:03:49,185 --> 00:03:53,068
Fear of hidden powers can push
even a believer toward harshness.

70
00:03:53,518 --> 00:03:57,827
Panic and force are one extreme.
Careless superstition is the other.

71
00:03:58,277 --> 00:04:01,085
The quiet path is trust:
the Cross, prayer, the

72
00:04:01,085 --> 00:04:03,355
Holy Mysteries, and mercy to the weak.

73
00:04:03,805 --> 00:04:06,685
Tonight, give God one
fear, and sleep in peace.

74
00:04:08,635 --> 00:04:12,048
Tell us below: which version of
the chronicle do you believe?

75
00:04:12,498 --> 00:04:15,485
Follow for the next
story. This is Ethiopics.
